/T (Troubleshooting note: bastion SSH timeout)
/E (Troubleshooting note: bastion SSH timeout)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 94 0 R
/T (At first ssh ewb-bastion timed out even though my SG rule contained the IP shown by checkip.amazonaws.com. My network reaches IPv4 hosts through carrier NAT, so the bastion saw a different source address. I temporarily widened the rule to find the address, read it on the bastion with journalctl -u sshd \(it was 152.59.62.39\), and then narrowed the rule to 152.59.62.39/32. The rule is never opened to 0.0.0.0/0.)
/E (At first ssh ewb-bastion timed out even though my SG rule contained the IP shown by checkip.amazonaws.com. My network reaches IPv4 hosts through carrier NAT, so the bastion saw a different source address. I temporarily widened the rule to find the address, read it on the bastion with journalctl -u sshd \(it was 152.59.62.39\), and then narrowed the rule to 152.59.62.39/32. The rule is never opened to 0.0.0.0/0.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
